            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0499" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.51/611a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-30T17:00:00-05:00">January 30, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>77. Please endeavor, through discreet inquiry, to ascertain (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) whether British banks or firms are now extending
                    credits, short term or otherwise, to Japanese interests, (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the method employed to “peg” the yen to the
                    pound sterling and (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) if the method employed is
                    the maintenance of gold or other deposits in British banks, whether credits are
                    extended thereon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
